This pull request aims to implement the parsing of symbolic links. In an `.asar` file's header JSON, a link looks like this:

```json
"file" {
  "link": "path/to/actual/file.txt"
}
```

[Symbolic links](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Symbolic_link) in an `.asar` file don't have the same structure as files do whatsoever, they only have a `link` field. In combination with the path, this information can be used to create an actual symbolic link.

```rs
// on unix
std::os::unix::fs::symlink(link, path);

// on windows
std::os::windows::fs::symlink_file(link, path);
// or
std::os::windows::fs::symlink_dir(link, path);
```

